Rem ==================================================================
Rem devils-dust.shoddy — Devil's Dust on the scribbler (window + loop).
Rem
Rem Run: mill run mills/devils-dust/devils-dust.shoddy
Rem      Wool in the air of a shoddy mill: wisps flocking by the three
Rem      boids rules while the devil's drum turns below — and a tuning
Rem      panel to reshape the storm while it blows.
Rem
Rem Panel controls (mouse): click a tab to switch groups, click or drag
Rem a slider to set it. The button row is the machine's speed lever,
Rem left to right: four lever POSITIONS, each a preset of knob values
Rem the machine winds to, sliders turning as it goes. SLOW is the
Rem gentle end (speeds and drum at about a third, loft kept — the sky
Rem never empties), NORMAL is the frozen defaults, MAX is every knob at
Rem its rail — the loudest legal setting — and ELEVEN is every knob at
Rem a quarter past its rail (Spinal Tap owns the rest of that
Rem sentence). Below the lever, the red STOP bar is the emergency stop:
Rem most of the drive dies in the instant of the pull, the rest coasts
Rem down, and the wool settles where it falls. The position the goal
Rem sits on lights up. X hides the panel, the PANEL [H] hint brings it
Rem back.
Rem (Keyboard): 1-4 or Tab switch groups, Up/Down pick a knob,
Rem Left/Right nudge it (Shift for coarse), H hides or shows the panel,
Rem S slow, N normal, M max, E eleven, 0/Space full stop, B mutes the
Rem mill (a MUTED lamp shows on the footer). Q or Escape quits.
Rem
Rem The devil is HEARD as well as seen — devils-dust-sound.shoddy gives
Rem it a deep polyphonic drone, a rev thump, and lever gestures, all
Rem read from the live Tune, so the machine's inertia is audible: the
Rem pitch climbs as the belt loads and dies away on a STOP coast.
Rem
Rem The pure model — the flock, the steering, the step, and the knob
Rem TABLE the panel reflects — is in devils-dust-core.shoddy and is
Rem unit-tested headless. This file is the window half: the mill
Rem interior, the devil silhouette, the wisp trails, the panel, and the
Rem event loop. Frames come from ScribblerTick at a fixed FPS (SetFps),
Rem so the loop sits at zero CPU between frames. Every branch of Loop's
Rem Select Case calls Loop directly (or closes) — a genuine SELF tail
Rem call, which CodeGen turns into a loop.
Rem
Rem The Studio record is the whole app: the Dust (which carries its own
Rem Knobs) plus the Panel's UI state. Every input handler is a pure
Rem Studio -> Studio function; the panel never touches the model except
Rem through KnobGet/KnobSet on the table.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "devils-dust-core.shoddy"
Include "devils-dust-sound.shoddy"
Include "scribbler.shoddy"
Include "math.shoddy"
Include "keys.shoddy"
Include "buzzer.shoddy"

Rem ---- app state -----------------------------------------------------

Type Panel
    PTab  As Number          Rem which tab is open, 1..4
    PRow  As Number          Rem which knob row is selected on that tab
    PShow As Boolean
    PDrag As Boolean         Rem a slider is being mouse-dragged

Def NewPanel() As Panel
    Panel(1, 1, True, False)

Type Studio
    Sd    As Dust
    Sp    As Panel
    SFps  As Number          Rem measured frame rate, smoothed
    SThru As Number          Rem wool through the devil per second, smoothed
    SAt   As Number          Rem previous tick timestamp; 0 = no tick yet
    SGoal As Knobs           Rem where the levers are set; Tune winds toward it
    SHz   As Number          Rem drone Hz last sent to the buzzer; 0 = gated off
    SMute As Boolean         Rem B key: the mill runs silent

Rem One frame of sound, or enforced silence. AllQuiet is idempotent,
Rem so a muted mill costs three no-op words a frame.
Def MillTick(st As Studio, d2 As Dust) As Number
    If SMute(st) Then
        AllQuiet(SHz(st))
    Else
        MillVoice(Sd(st), d2, SHz(st))

Rem The machine's inertia: the fraction of the remaining distance to
Rem the goal covered each frame. Tons of iron on a belt drive take a
Rem few seconds from lever-pull to full change.
Def GlideT() As Number
    0.02

Rem ---- panel geometry ------------------------------------------------

Def PanX() As Number
    WorldW() - 372
Def PanY() As Number
    14
Def PanW() As Number
    358
Def TabH() As Number
    24
Def TabW() As Number
    76
Def RowH() As Number
    30
Def TrackW() As Number
    PanW() - 20
Def RowsY() As Number
    PanY() + TabH() + 8
Def PanH(tab As Number) As Number
    TabH() + 12 + KnobRows(tab) * RowH() + 46

Rem The button row, below the last slider — the machine's speed lever,
Rem left to right in increasing fury: SLOW, NORMAL, MAX, ELEVEN. Four
Rem equal buttons filling the panel's inner width, evenly gapped.
Def BtnY(tab As Number) As Number
    RowsY() + KnobRows(tab) * RowH()
Def BtnW() As Number
    80
Def BtnSx() As Number
    PanX() + 10
Def BtnNx() As Number
    BtnSx() + BtnW() + 6
Def BtnMx() As Number
    BtnNx() + BtnW() + 6
Def BtnEx() As Number
    BtnMx() + BtnW() + 6

Rem The emergency stop: a full-width red bar below the lever.
Def StopY(tab As Number) As Number
    BtnY(tab) + 22

Rem ---- wisps ---------------------------------------------------------

Rem Brightness of trail segment k (1 = newest). Older wool fades.
Def Fade(k As Number) As Number
    Nth({ 95, 70, 50, 33, 18 }, Min(k, 5)) / 100

Def Shade(c As Number, k As Number) As Number
    Round(c * Fade(k))

Def FiberSeg(sc As Scribbler, f As Fiber, x As Number, y As Number, knots As List Of Knot, k As Number) As Scribbler
    If IsEmpty(knots) Then
        sc
    Else
        Let q = First(knots)
        Let s = DrawLine(sc, Round(x), Round(y), Round(Kx(q)), Round(Ky(q)), Shade(Cr(f), k), Shade(Cg(f), k), Shade(Cb(f), k))
        FiberSeg(s, f, Kx(q), Ky(q), Rest(knots), k + 1)

Def DrawFiber(sc As Scribbler, f As Fiber) As Scribbler
    Let tail = FiberSeg(sc, f, Fx(f), Fy(f), Trail(f), 1)
    FillRect(tail, Round(Fx(f)) - 1, Round(Fy(f)) - 1, 2, 2, Cr(f), Cg(f), Cb(f))

Rem A speck of fine dust is a single warm-grey pixel, drawn behind the
Rem devil so the machine reads solid through the haze.
Def DrawMotes(sc As Scribbler, motes As List Of Mote) As Scribbler
    Fold(motes, sc, Fn(s, m) => ScribblerPixel(s, Round(Mx(m)), Round(My(m)), Mb(m), Mb(m) - 4, Mb(m) - 8))

Rem ---- the mill ------------------------------------------------------

Def DrawFloor(sc As Scribbler) As Scribbler
    Let strip = FillRect(sc, 0, FloorTop(), WorldW(), WorldH() - FloorTop(), 38, 33, 29)
    DrawHLine(strip, FloorTop() - 1, 0, WorldW() - 1, 60, 52, 46)

Rem One tooth on the drum: a spoke from mid-radius out past the rim,
Rem rotated by the drum angle.
Def DrawTooth(sc As Scribbler, turn As Number, k As Number) As Scribbler
    Let a = turn + k * Tau() / 8
    DrawLine(sc, Round(DevilX() + Cos(a) * DrumR() * 0.45), Round(DevilY() + Sin(a) * DrumR() * 0.45), Round(DevilX() + Cos(a) * (DrumR() + 6)), Round(DevilY() + Sin(a) * (DrumR() + 6)), 150, 142, 134)

Rem The devil in silhouette, mid-room: housing centred on the floor,
Rem feed hopper at its left shoulder, and the toothed drum exposed at
Rem the top centre — spraying wool to both sides, which is where
Rem RimFiber's upper arc sends it. Everything hangs off DevilX so the
Rem machine and the model can never drift apart.
Def DrawDevil(sc As Scribbler, turn As Number) As Scribbler
    Let housing = FillRect(sc, DevilX() - 99, FloorTop() - 90, 198, 90, 58, 54, 58)
    Let hedge = DrawRect(housing, DevilX() - 99, FloorTop() - 90, 198, 90, 96, 90, 96)
    Let hopper = FillRect(hedge, DevilX() - 93, FloorTop() - 130, 80, 42, 52, 48, 52)
    Let hopedge = DrawRect(hopper, DevilX() - 93, FloorTop() - 130, 80, 42, 96, 90, 96)
    Let barrel = FillCircle(hopedge, DevilX(), DevilY(), DrumR(), 74, 70, 78)
    Let rim = DrawCircle(barrel, DevilX(), DevilY(), DrumR(), 128, 120, 128)
    Fold(Range(0, 7), rim, Fn(s, k) => DrawTooth(s, turn, k))

Rem ---- the colour language -------------------------------------------
Rem One heat scale for the whole console, the same liveries as the
Rem lever: brick red at the bottom (stopped), mute yellow low (slow),
Rem mute green at normal, steel ivory at the legal top (max), ember
Rem past it (eleven). Sliders, meters and buttons all speak it.

Def MixDye(a As Dye, b As Dye, t As Number) As Dye
    Let u = Clamp(t, 0, 1)
    Dye(Round(Lerp(Dr(a), Dr(b), u)), Round(Lerp(Dg(a), Dg(b), u)), Round(Lerp(Db(a), Db(b), u)))

Rem Place v on the scale: lo is red, halfway to mid is yellow, mid is
Rem green, hi is ivory, and hot overrides everything with ember. The
Rem gauge anchors are deliberately more saturated than the button
Rem liveries — same hues, more chroma — a colour has to survive being
Rem five pixels tall.
Def HeatRamp(v As Number, lo As Number, mid As Number, hi As Number, hot As Boolean) As Dye
    If hot Then
        Dye(255, 102, 48)
    Else
        If v >= mid Then
            MixDye(Dye(96, 158, 82), Dye(236, 228, 206), Ifte(hi > mid, (v - mid) / (hi - mid), 1))
        Else
            Let u = Ifte(mid > lo, (v - lo) / (mid - lo), 1)
            If u < 0.5 Then
                MixDye(Dye(186, 58, 48), Dye(188, 158, 56), u * 2)
            Else
                MixDye(Dye(188, 158, 56), Dye(96, 158, 82), (u - 0.5) * 2)

Rem ---- the panel -----------------------------------------------------

Rem Where the slider fill sits for knob id, as a fraction of its rails.
Def KnobFrac(kb As Knobs, id As Number) As Number
    (KnobGet(kb, id) - KnobLo(id)) / (KnobHi(id) - KnobLo(id))

Rem A knob's value translated into the colour language: red toward its
Rem floor, green at its NORMAL default, ivory at its rail, ember past.
Def KnobDye(kb As Knobs, id As Number) As Dye
    HeatRamp(KnobGet(kb, id), KnobLo(id), KnobGet(NewKnobs(), id), KnobHi(id), KnobHot(kb, id))

Def DrawTab(sc As Scribbler, p As Panel, t As Number) As Scribbler
    Let x = PanX() + 4 + (t - 1) * (TabW() + 2)
    Let active = t = PTab(p)
    Let box = FillRect(sc, x, PanY() + 4, TabW(), TabH() - 8, Ifte(active, 188, 46), Ifte(active, 178, 42), Ifte(active, 158, 40))
    ScribblerText(box, x + Round((TabW() - Len(TabName(t)) * 8) / 2), PanY() + 8, 1, Ifte(active, 40, 150), Ifte(active, 36, 142), Ifte(active, 34, 132), TabName(t))

Rem One knob row: name, value, slider track, fill, and handle. The
Rem selected row draws brighter; the fill is kept at least a pixel so
Rem the track never reads as empty. The handle is the LEVER — it sits
Rem at the goal and moves the instant you set it; the fill and the
Rem value are the MACHINE, winding toward it at the pace of iron.
Rem The track is guarded: fill and handle clamp at the rail no matter
Rem the value. Fill, value and handle wear the heat colour of what they
Rem show — the fill and value the machine's, the handle the goal's — so
Rem a gauge past its rail burns ember, unmistakable next to MAX's legal
Rem ivory. It's max... or eleven.
Def DrawKnobRow(sc As Scribbler, kb As Knobs, goal As Knobs, p As Panel, row As Number) As Scribbler
    Let id = KnobId(PTab(p), row)
    Let y = RowsY() + (row - 1) * RowH()
    Let sel = row = PRow(p)
    Let heat = KnobDye(kb, id)
    Let gleam = KnobDye(goal, id)
    Let name = ScribblerText(sc, PanX() + 10, y, 1, Ifte(sel, 235, 150), Ifte(sel, 226, 142), Ifte(sel, 210, 132), KnobName(id))
    Let vink = MixDye(heat, Dye(255, 255, 255), 0.1)
    Let vtxt = ScribblerText(name, PanX() + PanW() - 66, y, 1, Dr(vink), Dg(vink), Db(vink), PadL(Str(RoundTo(KnobGet(kb, id), 3)), 7))
    Let track = FillRect(vtxt, PanX() + 10, y + 13, TrackW(), 5, 58, 52, 48)
    Let fw = Clamp(Round(KnobFrac(kb, id) * TrackW()), 1, TrackW())
    Let gw = Clamp(Round(KnobFrac(goal, id) * TrackW()), 1, TrackW())
    Let fill = FillRect(track, PanX() + 10, y + 13, fw, 5, Dr(heat), Dg(heat), Db(heat))
    Let lever = MixDye(gleam, Dye(255, 255, 255), Ifte(sel, 0.45, 0.2))
    FillRect(fill, PanX() + 9 + gw, y + 10, 3, 11, Dr(lever), Dg(lever), Db(lever))

Rem A panel button in its own livery: dimmed to embers when idle, full
Rem colour when the lever sits on it (text goes dark for contrast).
Def DrawBtn(sc As Scribbler, x As Number, w As Number, y As Number, lit As Boolean, r As Number, g As Number, b As Number, label As String) As Scribbler
    Let box = FillRect(sc, x, y, w, 16, Ifte(lit, r, Round(r * 0.35)), Ifte(lit, g, Round(g * 0.35)), Ifte(lit, b, Round(b * 0.35)))
    Let edge = DrawRect(box, x, y, w, 16, 104, 96, 88)
    ScribblerText(edge, x + Round((w - Len(label) * 8) / 2), y + 4, 1, Ifte(lit, 36, Round(r * 0.8)), Ifte(lit, 32, Round(g * 0.8)), Ifte(lit, 30, Round(b * 0.8)), label)

Def DrawPanel(sc As Scribbler, st As Studio) As Scribbler
    Let p = Sp(st)
    If Not PShow(p) Then
        ScribblerText(sc, WorldW() - 108, 16, 1, 110, 102, 94, "PANEL [H]")
    Else
        Let kb = Tune(Sd(st))
        Let goal = SGoal(st)
        Let bg = FillRect(sc, PanX(), PanY(), PanW(), PanH(PTab(p)), 27, 24, 22)
        Let border = DrawRect(bg, PanX(), PanY(), PanW(), PanH(PTab(p)), 104, 96, 88)
        Let tabs = Fold(Range(1, 4), border, Fn(s, t) => DrawTab(s, p, t))
        Let xbox = ScribblerText(tabs, PanX() + PanW() - 16, PanY() + 8, 1, 168, 110, 100, "X")
        Rem The lever position the goal sits on lights up; hand-tuned
        Rem sliders light nothing. Liveries: SLOW mute yellow, NORMAL
        Rem mute green, MAX steel ivory (the gauge's legal full-white),
        Rem ELEVEN ember (the gauges' overload glow), STOP brick red on
        Rem its own full-width bar.
        Let rows = Fold(Range(1, KnobRows(PTab(p))), xbox, Fn(s, r) => DrawKnobRow(s, kb, goal, p, r))
        Let b1 = DrawBtn(rows, BtnSx(), BtnW(), BtnY(PTab(p)), KnobsMatch(goal, SlowKnobs()), 158, 138, 64, "SLOW [S]")
        Let b2 = DrawBtn(b1, BtnNx(), BtnW(), BtnY(PTab(p)), KnobsMatch(goal, NewKnobs()), 96, 134, 80, "NORMAL [N]")
        Let b3 = DrawBtn(b2, BtnMx(), BtnW(), BtnY(PTab(p)), KnobsMatch(goal, MaxKnobs()), 176, 168, 152, "MAX [M]")
        Let b4 = DrawBtn(b3, BtnEx(), BtnW(), BtnY(PTab(p)), KnobsMatch(goal, ElevenKnobs()), 214, 92, 54, "ELEVEN [E]")
        DrawBtn(b4, BtnSx(), PanW() - 20, StopY(PTab(p)), KnobsMatch(goal, StopKnobs()), 168, 64, 56, "STOP [0]")

Rem ---- input: keyboard -----------------------------------------------

Rem Every control writes the GOAL; the live Tune chases it each tick.
Rem Slider input goes through KnobSet, so hands clamp at the rails —
Rem only ELEVEN's constructor reaches past them.
Def PutKnob(st As Studio, id As Number, v As Number) As Studio
    With(st, SGoal = KnobSet(SGoal(st), id, v))

Rem The five lever positions. Each sets the GOAL; the machine winds its
Rem values there at the pace of iron, sliders turning as it goes. Each
Rem pull also speaks — a short low phrase on channel 5 — unless the
Rem mill is muted, in which case the branch that plays nothing is taken
Rem whole (Ifte is eager, so a sound call can never hide inside one).

Rem Gentle values, loft kept — slow wool is still flying wool.
Def GoSlow(st As Studio) As Studio
    If SMute(st) Then
        With(st, SGoal = SlowKnobs())
    Else
        Play(5, "T90 O2 L8 E C")
        With(st, SGoal = SlowKnobs())

Rem Every lever back to the frozen defaults — the N key and the panel's
Rem NORMAL button both land here.
Def GoNormal(st As Studio) As Studio
    If SMute(st) Then
        With(st, SGoal = NewKnobs())
    Else
        Play(5, "T120 O2 L8 G E C")
        With(st, SGoal = NewKnobs())

Rem Everything the panel can legally give.
Def GoMax(st As Studio) As Studio
    If SMute(st) Then
        With(st, SGoal = MaxKnobs())
    Else
        Play(5, "T140 O2 L8 C E G > C")
        With(st, SGoal = MaxKnobs())

Rem One louder. The riff climbs by semitones — of course it does.
Def GoEleven(st As Studio) As Studio
    If SMute(st) Then
        With(st, SGoal = ElevenKnobs())
    Else
        Play(5, "T160 O2 L16 C C# D D# E8")
        With(st, SGoal = ElevenKnobs())

Rem The emergency stop. Throwing the belt off is not a glide: most of
Rem the drive vanishes in the instant of the pull (the one-time 0.7
Rem cut), then what momentum is left coasts down through the usual
Rem winding. Quick, but the drum still visibly runs down rather than
Rem freezing mid-turn. The slap is the belt hitting the floor; the
Rem drone's dying fall follows on its own.
Def GoStop(st As Studio) As Studio
    Let cut = With(Sd(st), Tune = BlendKnobs(Tune(Sd(st)), StopKnobs(), 0.7))
    If SMute(st) Then
        With(st, Sd = cut, SGoal = StopKnobs())
    Else
        SoundQueue(5, 55, 70)
        SoundQueue(5, 38, 140)
        With(st, Sd = cut, SGoal = StopKnobs())

Def SetTab(st As Studio, t As Number) As Studio
    Let p = With(Sp(st), PTab = Clamp(t, 1, 4))
    With(st, Sp = With(p, PRow = Clamp(PRow(p), 1, KnobRows(PTab(p)))))

Def MoveSel(st As Studio, dir As Number) As Studio
    Let p = Sp(st)
    With(st, Sp = With(p, PRow = Clamp(PRow(p) + dir, 1, KnobRows(PTab(p)))))

Rem Left/Right steps the knob by a fiftieth of its rails; Shift (bit 1
Rem of Mods) makes the step five times coarser.
Def NudgeKnob(st As Studio, dir As Number, mods As Number) As Studio
    Let p = Sp(st)
    Let id = KnobId(PTab(p), PRow(p))
    Let stp = (KnobHi(id) - KnobLo(id)) / 50 * Ifte(mods Mod 2 >= 1, 5, 1)
    PutKnob(st, id, KnobGet(SGoal(st), id) + dir * stp)

Def OnKey(st As Studio, gk As GameKey, mods As Number) As Studio
    Select Case gk
        Case ArrowUp
            MoveSel(st, -1)
        Case ArrowDown
            MoveSel(st, 1)
        Case ArrowLeft
            NudgeKnob(st, -1, mods)
        Case ArrowRight
            NudgeKnob(st, 1, mods)
        Case TabKey
            SetTab(st, Ifte(PTab(Sp(st)) = 4, 1, PTab(Sp(st)) + 1))
        Case CharKey(c) Where c >= 49 And c <= 52
            SetTab(st, c - 48)
        Case CharKey(c) Where c = Asc("H")
            With(st, Sp = With(Sp(st), PShow = Not PShow(Sp(st))))
        Case CharKey(c) Where c = Asc("S")
            GoSlow(st)
        Case CharKey(c) Where c = Asc("N")
            GoNormal(st)
        Case CharKey(c) Where c = Asc("M")
            GoMax(st)
        Case CharKey(c) Where c = Asc("E")
            GoEleven(st)
        Case CharKey(c) Where c = 48
            GoStop(st)
        Case SpaceBar
            GoStop(st)
        Case CharKey(c) Where c = Asc("B")
            With(st, SMute = Not SMute(st))
        Case Else
            st

Rem ---- input: mouse --------------------------------------------------

Def RowAt(y As Number) As Number
    Floor((y - RowsY()) / RowH()) + 1

Rem Set the selected knob from a mouse x on its slider track.
Def SlideTo(st As Studio, x As Number) As Studio
    Let p = Sp(st)
    Let id = KnobId(PTab(p), PRow(p))
    Let frac = Clamp((x - (PanX() + 10)) / TrackW(), 0, 1)
    PutKnob(st, id, KnobLo(id) + frac * (KnobHi(id) - KnobLo(id)))

Rem A click lands on the hidden-panel hint, the tab bar (a tab or the X
Rem close box), or a knob row — which selects it, starts a drag, and
Rem jumps the slider to the click.
Def OnClick(st As Studio, x As Number, y As Number) As Studio
    Let p = Sp(st)
    If Not PShow(p) Then
        If x > WorldW() - 116 And y < 32 Then
            With(st, Sp = With(p, PShow = True))
        Else
            st
    Else
        If x < PanX() Or x > PanX() + PanW() Or y < PanY() Or y > PanY() + PanH(PTab(p)) Then
            st
        Else
            If y < PanY() + TabH() Then
                If x > PanX() + PanW() - 24 Then
                    With(st, Sp = With(p, PShow = False))
                Else
                    SetTab(st, Clamp(Floor((x - PanX() - 4) / (TabW() + 2)) + 1, 1, 4))
            Else
                If RowAt(y) >= 1 And RowAt(y) <= KnobRows(PTab(p)) Then
                    SlideTo(With(st, Sp = With(p, PRow = RowAt(y), PDrag = True)), x)
                Else
                    If y >= BtnY(PTab(p)) And y <= BtnY(PTab(p)) + 16 Then
                        OnButtons(st, x)
                    Else
                        If y >= StopY(PTab(p)) And y <= StopY(PTab(p)) + 16 Then
                            GoStop(st)
                        Else
                            st

Rem Which of the four buttons a click in the button row landed on.
Def OnButtons(st As Studio, x As Number) As Studio
    If x >= BtnSx() And x <= BtnSx() + BtnW() Then
        GoSlow(st)
    Else
        If x >= BtnNx() And x <= BtnNx() + BtnW() Then
            GoNormal(st)
        Else
            If x >= BtnMx() And x <= BtnMx() + BtnW() Then
                GoMax(st)
            Else
                If x >= BtnEx() And x <= BtnEx() + BtnW() Then
                    GoEleven(st)
                Else
                    st

Def OnMove(st As Studio, x As Number) As Studio
    If PDrag(Sp(st)) Then
        SlideTo(st, x)
    Else
        st

Rem ---- number formatting ---------------------------------------------
Rem The font is monospace, so fixed-width fields keep the readouts from
Rem jittering as values change size: PadL right-aligns in a field of n,
Rem Fixed always shows exactly p decimals ("0.40", never "0.4").

Def PadL(s As String, n As Number) As String
    If Len(s) >= n Then
        s
    Else
        PadL(" " & s, n)

Def PadZ(s As String, n As Number) As String
    If Len(s) >= n Then
        s
    Else
        PadZ("0" & s, n)

Def Fixed(x As Number, p As Number) As String
    Let s = 10 ^ p
    Let n = Round(x * s)
    Str(Fix(n / s)) & "." & PadZ(Str(Abs(n Mod s)), p)

Rem ---- the footer ----------------------------------------------------
Rem The meters, one line on the floor strip: measured FPS, the
Rem lifecycle census, the flocking order parameter, mean speed, mean
Rem altitude, and wool through the devil per second. Census, order,
Rem speed and altitude are pure reads from the core; FPS and throughput
Rem are the two smoothed numbers Studio carries. Each meter wears the
Rem heat colour of its own reading — label dimmed, value full — so the
Rem footer reads like a row of gauges: a red ALOFT is an empty sky, a
Rem green FPS is a healthy clock, an ember SPEED is eleven's doing.

Def Meter(sc As Scribbler, x As Number, label As String, val As String, d As Dye) As Scribbler
    Let lab = ScribblerText(sc, x, FloorTop() + 7, 1, Round(Dr(d) * 0.62), Round(Dg(d) * 0.62), Round(Db(d) * 0.62), label)
    ScribblerText(lab, x + Len(label) * 8, FloorTop() + 7, 1, Dr(d), Dg(d), Db(d), val)

Def DrawFooter(sc As Scribbler, st As Studio) As Scribbler
    Let flock = Fibers(Sd(st))
    Let kb = Tune(Sd(st))
    Let c = TakeCensus(flock)
    Let want = FiberCount(kb)
    Let spd = MeanSpeed(flock)
    Let x0 = Round((WorldW() - 736) / 2)
    Let m1 = Meter(sc, x0, "FPS ", PadL(Str(Round(SFps(st))), 3), HeatRamp(SFps(st), 0, 30, 34, False))
    Let m2 = Meter(m1, x0 + 80, "ALOFT ", PadL(Str(Aloft(c)), 3), HeatRamp(Aloft(c), 0, want * 0.7, want, False))
    Let m3 = Meter(m2, x0 + 176, "RAIN ", PadL(Str(Raining(c)), 3), HeatRamp(Raining(c), 0, want * 0.2, want, False))
    Let m4 = Meter(m3, x0 + 264, "DOWN ", PadL(Str(Landed(c)), 3), HeatRamp(Landed(c), 0, want * 0.03, want, False))
    Let m5 = Meter(m4, x0 + 352, "ORDER ", Fixed(OrderParam(flock), 2), HeatRamp(OrderParam(flock), 0, 0.4, 1, False))
    Let m6 = Meter(m5, x0 + 456, "SPEED ", PadL(Fixed(spd, 1), 4), HeatRamp(spd, 0, 2, KnobHi(7), spd > KnobHi(7)))
    Let m7 = Meter(m6, x0 + 560, "ALT ", PadL(Str(Round(Altitude(flock))), 3), HeatRamp(Altitude(flock), 0, 300, FloorY(), False))
    Let m8 = Meter(m7, x0 + 640, "THRU ", PadL(Fixed(SThru(st), 1), 5) & "/S", HeatRamp(SThru(st), 0, 5, 25, False))
    If SMute(st) Then
        ScribblerText(m8, WorldW() - 62, FloorTop() + 7, 1, 186, 58, 48, "MUTED")
    Else
        m8

Rem ---- drawing the frame ---------------------------------------------

Def Draw(sc As Scribbler, st As Studio) As Scribbler
    Let d = Sd(st)
    Let bg = ScribblerFill(sc, 22, 19, 17)
    Let fl = DrawFloor(bg)
    Let haze = DrawMotes(fl, Motes(d))
    Let dv = DrawDevil(haze, Whirl(d))
    Let wool = Fold(Fibers(d), dv, DrawFiber)
    Let t1 = ScribblerText(wool, 20, 16, 3, 128, 118, 108, "DEVIL'S DUST")
    Let t2 = ScribblerText(t1, 20, 46, 2, 84, 78, 72, "WOOL IN THE AIR OF A SHODDY MILL - H PANEL, Q QUITS")
    ScribblerBlit(DrawPanel(DrawFooter(t2, st), st))

Rem ---- the loop ------------------------------------------------------

Rem Silence everything still sounding, then close the window. The
Rem lastHz of 1 forces the NoteOffs whether or not a drone was held.
Def CloseDown(sc As Scribbler) As Scribbler
    Let z = AllQuiet(1)
    ScribblerClose(sc)

Def Loop(sc As Scribbler, st As Studio) As Scribbler
    Select Case NextEvent(sc)
        Case ScribblerTick(at)
            Rem The machine winds toward its levers first (BlendKnobs),
            Rem then the frame steps. The FPS sample guards its own
            Rem first frame (SAt = 0) and division (Clamp floors the
            Rem delta at 1ms); throughput smooths harder because
            Rem respawns arrive 0-2 at a time.
            Let tuned = With(Sd(st), Tune = BlendKnobs(Tune(Sd(st)), SGoal(st), GlideT()))
            Let d2 = Advance(tuned)
            Let hz2 = MillTick(st, d2)
            Let samp = Ifte(SAt(st) = 0, SFps(st), 1000 / Clamp(at - SAt(st), 1, 1000))
            Let thru2 = Ifte(SAt(st) = 0, 0, SThru(st) + 0.05 * (FreshCount(Fibers(d2)) * samp - SThru(st)))
            Let st2 = With(st, Sd = d2, SFps = SFps(st) + 0.1 * (samp - SFps(st)), SThru = thru2, SAt = at, SHz = hz2)
            Loop(Draw(sc, st2), st2)
        Case ScribblerKeyDown(key, mods, at)
            If key = 27 Or key = Asc("Q") Then
                CloseDown(sc)
            Else
                Loop(sc, OnKey(st, ClassifyKey(key), mods))
        Case ScribblerMouseDown(x, y, btn, mods, at)
            Loop(sc, OnClick(st, x, y))
        Case ScribblerMouseMove(x, y, mods, at)
            Loop(sc, OnMove(st, x))
        Case ScribblerMouseUp(x, y, btn, mods, at)
            Loop(sc, With(st, Sp = With(Sp(st), PDrag = False)))
        Case ScribblerQuit
            CloseDown(sc)
        Case Else
            Loop(sc, st)

Def Main()
    Let sc0 = ScribblerOpen(WorldW(), WorldH())
    Let sc1 = ScribblerTitle(sc0, "Devil's Dust")
    Let sc2 = SetFps(sc1, 30)
    Print("Devil's Dust - wool in the air of a shoddy mill.")
    Print("Panel: 1-4/Tab pick a group, Up/Down pick a knob, Left/Right nudge")
    Print("(Shift = coarse), or click and drag the sliders. H panel. Speed")
    Print("lever: S slow, N normal, M max, E goes to eleven; 0 or Space is the")
    Print("full stop. B mutes the mill. Q or Escape quits.")
    SoundGain(5, 0.3)
    Let st = Studio(NewDust(), NewPanel(), 30, 0, 0, NewKnobs(), 0, False)
    Let done = Loop(Draw(sc2, st), st)
    Print("the mill rests")
